-The adapter is intentionally single-thread-affine and blocking. OpenSSL's error
-classification depends on the current thread's error queue and immediate
-`SSL_get_error()` call. If a record call reaches `SSL_ERROR_WANT_READ` or
-`SSL_ERROR_WANT_WRITE`, the adapter does not attempt to turn a one-shot API into
-an implicit event loop; it fails and poisons the channel. A production async
-transport should own an explicit resumable I/O state machine and retry the exact
-OpenSSL operation with the required arguments.
-
