+nontransferable guard shape, test-only capability linkage, preclaim policy,
+receipt terminality, and runtime negative cases. They are explicitly labeled
+**lexical hygiene, not semantic proof**.
+
+The complete registry caught a package-verifier omission: the strengthened
+atomic-publication audit required the new restart-reconciliation test, but the
+release verifier did not. The verifier now requires the complete rev0878 source,
+test, audit, and design-record surface rather than weakening the audit.
+
+The build graph remains wasteful. CMake contains 75 literal libraries, 96
+executables, and 188 literal `add_test` calls, yet semantic centers still include
+approximately 15,167 lines in `sync_domain.cpp`, 9,601 in
+`sync_domain_selftests.cpp`, 4,529 in `sqlite_replay_ledger.cpp`, and 3,713 in the
+causal SQLite owner. The full rebuild spends far more time compiling these older
+monoliths than the new authority slice. Target count has outpaced semantic
+modularity.
+
+Correction should proceed by authority boundary rather than arbitrary file size:
+
+- split restore/attestation, transition, serialization, and storage ownership;
+- generate repetitive target, sanitizer, and test wiring through CMake helpers;
+- retain a fast affected-authority gate plus one complete periodic registry;
